-- The lobby: a closed-off corner of a dead mall (docs/plans/lobby-rework.md,
-- "The place"; the owner, 2026-10-15). LB1a's grey-box layout, for walking
-- and judging before anything is modelled: World/MallBuilder builds it,
-- Logic/MallLayout checks it.
--
-- Studs, on the floor plan from the court's middle: x east, z south (the
-- spawn looks north at the video store), y up from the court floor. A room
-- is {x0, z0, x1, z1}; each builds its own walls just inside its rectangle.
-- A door stands on the line two rooms share (`runs` is the way that line
-- goes) and cuts both their walls; one with no `b` opens to outside and is
-- filled (`fill`).
--
-- The hall reads end to end: the diner closes its west end (the owner's
-- place for it), the giant shutter its east end, where the dead mall goes
-- on in the dark behind the grille. The video store's back door is the
-- only way into the garage, where the squads leave.
--
-- The story (the owner, after the first grey box: "an abandoned mall with a
-- secret community of investigators in it"): the mall died and its lamps
-- with it. The investigators came in through the loading dock, which is
-- their garage now, and run a generator there. Its cables go through the
-- video store's back door and out over the court's floor to the few places
-- they've opened again (the four shops, the diner) and to the mall's old ad
-- lightboxes, so those are what's lit. Their strings of bulbs mark the ways
-- they use; their tape and cardboard signs are on everything. The rest is
-- as the mall was left: dust sheets, a dry fountain, fallen ceiling tiles, a
-- bucket under a leak, the main doors boarded and chained, and the dead
-- mall taped off behind the shutter.

